  "notes": "Common direct rewrites are emitted for model methods, validators, and field/constrained-type kwargs; manual follow-up is still required for class-based Config -> model_config/ConfigDict conversion, `from_orm`/`orm_mode`, root-model migration, `parse_file`, `parse_obj_as`, and removed or behavior-changing kwargs such as `const`, `unique_items`, and `allow_mutation`.\nGrounded in the Pydantic 2.0 migration guide at https://docs.pydantic.dev/2.0/migration/. This packet only emits documented successors and direct surface rewrites: BaseModel serialization/validation methods, validator decorators, BaseSettings relocation, Config\u2192model_config, key attribute renames, and Field kwarg renames/drops. APIs that need structural refactors or have no one-step successor (for example __root__ models, parse_file, schema_json, parse_obj_as) are left to side_effects/manual review rather than guessed.",
